# HBC Sanyard — preserve live data & config

Production web root: `/var/www/hbcsanyard.veerlabs.solutions`

## Never overwrite on the live site

- Entire `data/` tree (`rwa.db`, receipts, vault, info-centre, messages, smtp/vapid/ai env, …)
- `share/` (Info Centre OG cards)
- CMS brand uploads: `assets/site/`
- Live catalog unless explicitly overriding: `projects.json`, `projects-public.json`, `catalog-exclusions.json`
- Runtime secrets: `data/smtp.env`, `data/vapid.env`, `data/ai.env`, `/etc/veercanvas/hbcsanyard.env`
- Do not push laptop `site.config.json` over the server (deploy already excludes it)

## Required deploy posture

```bash
# Safe (default): pulls live site-meta/catalog first, protects data/
SITE_ID=hbcsanyard EC2_KEY=… ./deploy/remote-deploy.sh

# ❌ Do not use unless the user explicitly asks
OVERRIDE_CATALOG=1 …
```

- Prefer `remote-deploy.sh` over ad-hoc `rsync --delete` to the web root.
- For AuthBuddy: merge only `auth.*` from local `site.config.json` into pulled live `site-meta.json` — never replace branding/CMS keys from a stale laptop copy.
- Seed/migrate DB columns in place (`init_rwa_db` / app boot); never replace `data/rwa.db` with a local file.

## Repo sync (veer-canvas ↔ hbcsanyard git)

When copying `sites/hbcsanyard/` into the standalone `hbcsanyard` repo (or the reverse):

```bash
# Always exclude runtime data / secrets
rsync -a --exclude 'data/' --exclude 'venv/' --exclude '.git' …
```

Never commit production `data/`, `*.env` (non-example), or SQLite DBs.
